.TH SEALED\-RUN 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.3.3" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
sealed\-run \- the agent\-facing boundary. Runs a pipeline of blocktools tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
sealed\-run agent|human '<pipeline>': run an allowlisted tool pipeline; agent mode prints only redacted output
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
WITHOUT a shell (no expansion, no injection), then:
.nf
.RS 2
  sealed\-run agent '<pipeline>'  \-> stdout = redacted public JSON lines only
  sealed\-run human '<pipeline>'  \-> raw output (keys!) to /dev/tty after a typed code
  sealed\-run pin\-tty             \-> pin this terminal session; afterwards codes are accepted only from it
  sealed\-run unpack /in|/secrets  \-> (wrapper, via `docker exec \-u 0`) unpack a tar from stdin into that
                                     tmpfs: files 0444 / dirs 0555 owned by root, so uid 10001 can read
                                     but never change them; the root dir is opened (0555) last
  sealed\-run staged agent|human '<pipeline>' \-> wait until /secrets is readable (staging done), then run
.RE
.fi
Pipeline grammar: `tool args... [< file] | tool args... | ...`
Tokens are whitespace\-separated. Only tools that live next to sealed\-run and are
on the allowlist can be run. Tool stderr is discarded.
.SH OPTIONS
No flags. Input is read from stdin or the arguments shown in SYNOPSIS.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
.nf
.RS 2
  sealed\-run agent '<pipeline>'  \-> stdout = redacted public JSON lines only
  sealed\-run human '<pipeline>'  \-> raw output (keys!) to /dev/tty after a typed code
  sealed\-run unpack /in|/secrets  \-> (wrapper, via `docker exec \-u 0`) unpack a tar from stdin into that
  sealed\-run staged agent|human '<pipeline>' \-> wait until /secrets is readable (staging done), then run
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
2
last status unsupported
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ sealed\-run agent 'rm \-rf /'
# exit 2, last status: unsupported
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
This is the sealed boundary: ./blocktools run starts it inside the sealed, offline container.
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
